1
00:00:04,458 --> 00:00:05,458
Don't move.

2
00:00:20,208 --> 00:00:21,208
Hey, friends.

3
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:24,875
Where are you folks from?

4
00:00:26,416 --> 00:00:27,416
Just passing through.

5
00:00:28,041 --> 00:00:29,166
Who are you people?

6
00:00:33,375 --> 00:00:34,375
Just the two of you?

7
00:00:36,666 --> 00:00:38,458
Your buddy here looks awful.

8
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:40,875
Looks like a bad injury.

9
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:48,500
Did you guys run into some trouble?

10
00:00:49,791 --> 00:00:50,916
None of your business.

11
00:00:53,083 --> 00:00:54,083
A Kuan.

12
00:00:56,583 --> 00:00:57,583
Sorry.

13
00:00:58,083 --> 00:00:59,443
I need to check your temperatures.

14
00:01:00,708 --> 00:01:01,708
Just routine.

15
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:23,250
You're clear.

16
00:01:26,875 --> 00:01:27,875
Don't be afraid.

17
00:01:29,083 --> 00:01:30,458
We came out here

18
00:01:30,958 --> 00:01:31,958
to

19
00:01:32,916 --> 00:01:33,916
scavenge for supplies.

20
00:01:36,625 --> 00:01:38,000
Our camp is just up ahead.

21
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:40,750
About a fifteen-minute drive.

22
00:01:43,416 --> 00:01:45,916
Do you want to come
to our camp and rest up?

23
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:48,083
Appreciate the offer.

24
00:01:49,041 --> 00:01:50,041
But no thanks.

25
00:01:54,625 --> 00:01:55,625
We won't force you.

26
00:01:57,625 --> 00:01:59,541
But if you don't treat that wound soon,

27
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:01,270
it's definitely going to get infected.

28
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:05,916
He's got a point.

29
00:02:06,383 --> 00:02:09,186
Your wound really needs to be
properly treated as soon as possible.

30
00:02:16,416 --> 00:02:18,166
Then, sorry for the trouble.

31
00:02:32,333 --> 00:02:33,333
We're here.

32
00:02:40,833 --> 00:02:41,833
Brother Dao is back!

33
00:02:42,375 --> 00:02:43,375
I'm back!

34
00:02:44,041 --> 00:02:46,165
Open the gate! Brother Dao is back!

35
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,875
Boys, unload the cargo!

36
00:02:48,083 --> 00:02:49,083
You got it, boss!

37
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:55,750
What do you think?

38
00:02:56,375 --> 00:02:57,375
This place

39
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:00,000
used to be a movie studio.

40
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:03,083
Everyone fled before the apocalypse.

41
00:03:03,291 --> 00:03:04,541
We fixed it up a bit,

42
00:03:04,791 --> 00:03:05,958
and turned it into a base.

43
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,166
Now there are dozens of us living here.

44
00:03:08,791 --> 00:03:10,017
We've got elderly folks and kids.

45
00:03:10,041 --> 00:03:11,499
We all look out for each other.

46
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:12,517
Thanks for your hard work, Brother Dao.

47
00:03:12,541 --> 00:03:13,541
Good job out there.

48
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:16,500
Bet you didn't expect this.

49
00:03:16,916 --> 00:03:19,333
We all used to work in the film industry.

50
00:03:20,416 --> 00:03:21,416
As for me,

51
00:03:21,625 --> 00:03:22,916
I used to be a producer.

52
00:03:24,166 --> 00:03:25,166
That's Xiao Long.

53
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:27,000
He started out as a stuntman.

54
00:03:27,666 --> 00:03:29,500
Lao Jiang is a prop master.

55
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:32,582
Sister Li, keeping busy?

56
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:34,063
- Hey, Brother Dao.
- Hi, Brother Dao.

57
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:36,291
Sister Li used to be our costume designer.

58
00:03:37,166 --> 00:03:39,208
Everyone has their own talents.

59
00:03:39,625 --> 00:03:42,666
Who knew they'd all come
in handy after the apocalypse?

60
00:03:44,875 --> 00:03:45,875
Let me help you.

61
00:03:45,979 --> 00:03:47,729
Brother Dao is
back! Oh, no need.

62
00:03:48,416 --> 00:03:49,208
It's pretty heavy.

63
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:50,125
Thanks, Brother Dao.

64
00:03:50,125 --> 00:03:51,125
Don't mention it.

65
00:03:51,750 --> 00:03:52,915
I won!

66
00:03:52,916 --> 00:03:53,916
Playing mahjong?

67
00:03:54,166 --> 00:03:55,374
I'm out.

68
00:03:55,375 --> 00:03:56,375
Just playing a bit.

69
00:03:56,458 --> 00:03:57,208
Brother Dao.

70
00:03:57,208 --> 00:03:58,208
Just finished working.

71
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:01,625
We basically don't keep freeloaders here.

72
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:04,215
Those who can fight go
hunting and keep watch.

73
00:04:04,958 --> 00:04:07,023
Those who are good with their hands
cook and sew.

74
00:04:07,291 --> 00:04:07,958
Hello, Brother Dao.

75
00:04:07,958 --> 00:04:08,958
Hello.

76
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,458
That's our water storage area.

77
00:04:11,666 --> 00:04:13,666
Water for laundry and
cooking all comes from here.

78
00:04:14,416 --> 00:04:17,250
We also have some people
who can't do heavy lifting.

79
00:04:17,416 --> 00:04:20,708
So we have them help watch
the kids and grow vegetables.

80
00:04:21,291 --> 00:04:22,531
We all have to survive somehow.

81
00:04:23,708 --> 00:04:24,750
This is the infirmary.

82
00:04:25,291 --> 00:04:26,291
Hello, Brother Dao.

83
00:04:26,375 --> 00:04:27,832
Feeling better? Remember
to change your dressing.

84
00:04:27,833 --> 00:04:28,916
Will do! Much better.

85
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Xiao Xi.

86
00:04:30,791 --> 00:04:33,083
Make sure to get this
brother some antibiotics.

87
00:04:33,166 --> 00:04:34,166
Okay.

88
00:04:35,541 --> 00:04:38,000
You two can rest up for a few days.

89
00:04:38,625 --> 00:04:40,416
If you want to stay long-term,

90
00:04:40,875 --> 00:04:43,000
you'll have to pitch in
and work like everyone else.

91
00:04:43,708 --> 00:04:45,332
After all, the resources here

92
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:46,708
were scraped together bit by bit.

93
00:04:47,375 --> 00:04:48,875
No one gets a free ride.

94
00:04:53,583 --> 00:04:54,583
Thanks, Brother Dao.

95
00:04:54,833 --> 00:04:56,184
We'll just rest for a couple of days.

96
00:04:56,208 --> 00:04:57,448
We won't cause you any trouble.

97
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,375
Alright, no problem.

98
00:04:59,916 --> 00:05:00,916
Xiao Xi.

99
00:05:00,958 --> 00:05:02,438
Help me settle these two brothers in.

100
00:05:02,708 --> 00:05:04,290
Check the storeroom and see what

101
00:05:04,291 --> 00:05:05,666
daily necessities they might need.

102
00:05:06,208 --> 00:05:06,791
Please.

103
00:05:06,791 --> 00:05:07,791
Follow me.

104
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:12,958
Doudou, ride carefully! Don't fall!

105
00:05:16,541 --> 00:05:17,957
Your wound looks pretty bad.

106
00:05:17,958 --> 00:05:20,333
I'll have Doctor He from
our base take a look at it later.

107
00:05:20,666 --> 00:05:21,666
No need to trouble him.

108
00:05:22,041 --> 00:05:25,416
No way, that wound needs to be
properly cleaned and disinfected again.

109
00:05:25,875 --> 00:05:27,875
Could you grab some
iodine and gauze for us later?

110
00:05:28,291 --> 00:05:30,750
Sure. If you need anything
else, just tell Brother Dao.

111
00:05:31,875 --> 00:05:32,875
These two rooms are empty.

112
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:33,875
Take your pick.

113
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:35,750
One room is enough.

114
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,500
One room it is, then.

115
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:40,601
I'll have someone bring over
bedding and medicine shortly.

116
00:05:40,625 --> 00:05:41,625
Okay, thanks.

117
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,000
"The Last Oath"

118
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:53,100
(Episode 14: The Final Performance)

119
00:07:11,416 --> 00:07:12,416
Alright.

120
00:07:13,666 --> 00:07:14,791
Lights out.

121
00:07:15,291 --> 00:07:17,125
Everyone, please return to your rooms.

122
00:07:17,541 --> 00:07:18,661
Lock your doors and windows.

123
00:07:18,791 --> 00:07:19,791
Stay safe.

124
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:22,583
Lights out.

125
00:07:22,958 --> 00:07:24,790
Everyone, please return to your rooms.

126
00:07:24,791 --> 00:07:25,791
Get some sleep.

127
00:07:26,416 --> 00:07:27,416
Stay safe.

128
00:07:39,541 --> 00:07:40,541
Good night.

129
00:07:46,208 --> 00:07:47,333
Sleep here.

130
00:07:56,791 --> 00:07:57,875
Then behave yourself.

131
00:09:19,708 --> 00:09:21,208
Just go to sleep.

132
00:09:33,375 --> 00:09:34,375
Go to sleep.

133
00:10:03,416 --> 00:10:04,250
The weather is so nice today.

134
00:10:04,250 --> 00:10:05,250
Lin Zai!

135
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:08,500
Grandma Qiu!

136
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:14,041
Child, you're still alive!

137
00:10:14,708 --> 00:10:15,750
Wait, Grandma,

138
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,041
what are you doing here?

139
00:10:18,708 --> 00:10:19,708
A-Leh!

140
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,958
What happened to you guys?

141
00:10:23,250 --> 00:10:25,166
We all thought you were dead.

142
00:10:26,291 --> 00:10:28,375
Grandma, it's a long story.

143
00:10:29,833 --> 00:10:32,833
A-Leh and I did go out
to pick wild fruit that day,

144
00:10:32,916 --> 00:10:34,516
but we ran into some trouble on the way.

145
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:35,833
And then?

146
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
And then,

147
00:10:38,125 --> 00:10:39,125
thanks to A-Leh,

148
00:10:39,166 --> 00:10:40,366
he protected me the whole way.

149
00:10:46,041 --> 00:10:48,208
Grandma, why are you here?

150
00:10:49,125 --> 00:10:50,605
Where are Sister Chen and Brother Li?

151
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:56,458
I just got here two or three days ago.

152
00:10:57,541 --> 00:10:58,916
After you left,

153
00:10:59,625 --> 00:11:02,000
our base was attacked by zombies.

154
00:11:03,125 --> 00:11:05,708
Chen Jin and Li Ming
protected me as we ran this way.

155
00:11:06,083 --> 00:11:07,958
When we were almost at this camp,

156
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,750
we ran into a horde of zombies.

157
00:11:10,208 --> 00:11:11,749
They hid me away,

158
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:13,416
and went to lure the zombies off.

159
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,791
They never came back.

160
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Later,

161
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:23,458
the people from this camp found me,

162
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,500
and brought me back here.

163
00:11:27,375 --> 00:11:29,000
Where did you separate from them?

164
00:11:30,583 --> 00:11:31,833
Not far from here.

165
00:11:32,291 --> 00:11:34,000
An abandoned industrial zone.

166
00:11:34,250 --> 00:11:36,625
Let's go borrow a car and find them.

167
00:11:38,083 --> 00:11:39,332
Don't worry, Grandma.

168
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:40,833
I'll bring them both back.

169
00:11:43,666 --> 00:11:45,208
Be careful out there!

170
00:11:50,083 --> 00:11:52,416
Come on, everyone, line up!

171
00:11:53,041 --> 00:11:53,708
Thanks, brother.

172
00:11:53,708 --> 00:11:54,666
Come on, grab it yourselves.

173
00:11:54,666 --> 00:11:55,041
Take more if it's not enough.

174
00:11:55,042 --> 00:11:56,351
Come back for seconds
if you're still hungry.

175
00:11:56,375 --> 00:11:57,495
Grab it yourselves. Come on.

176
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,041
You're just in time. Food's ready.

177
00:12:01,208 --> 00:12:02,875
Xiao Xi, get them two trays.

178
00:12:04,208 --> 00:12:05,958
Hey, no cutting in line.

179
00:12:06,208 --> 00:12:07,768
You have to go to the back of the line.

180
00:12:08,708 --> 00:12:09,915
No need, Brother Dao.

181
00:12:09,916 --> 00:12:11,166
We're not here to eat.

182
00:12:11,291 --> 00:12:12,666
We have something to ask you.

183
00:12:14,625 --> 00:12:15,625
Go ahead.

184
00:12:16,333 --> 00:12:17,665
Grandma Qiu, who just arrived here,

185
00:12:17,666 --> 00:12:19,166
used to be in our camp.

186
00:12:19,208 --> 00:12:21,666
She got separated from two
others at the industrial zone.

187
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:22,875
We want to go look for them.

188
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:26,625
The industrial zone?

189
00:12:28,541 --> 00:12:30,061
There are a lot of zombies over there.

190
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:31,958
Are you sure you want to go?

191
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:33,892
We have to, no matter how dangerous it is.

192
00:12:36,688 --> 00:12:37,688
How about this?

193
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:40,041
I'll have A Cheng and A Kuan go with you.

194
00:12:40,208 --> 00:12:42,291
They know that area pretty well.

195
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,000
No need.

196
00:12:44,916 --> 00:12:46,166
You're still injured.

197
00:12:46,375 --> 00:12:47,875
Just lending us a car will be enough.

198
00:12:49,791 --> 00:12:51,111
You think you can just borrow it?

199
00:12:53,291 --> 00:12:55,750
We're not running a charity here.

200
00:12:58,375 --> 00:13:00,583
Brother Dao, we can pull our weight.

201
00:13:02,291 --> 00:13:03,666
I'm good at fixing electronics.

202
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,375
A-Leh can stand guard.

203
00:13:05,625 --> 00:13:07,458
Or scavenge for supplies.

204
00:13:08,250 --> 00:13:09,750
Please, just let us borrow the car.

205
00:13:26,458 --> 00:13:27,500
Thank you, Brother Dao.

206
00:14:19,416 --> 00:14:21,374
Warning: Elevated heart rate detected.

207
00:14:21,375 --> 00:14:23,375
Shut up, shut up!

208
00:14:24,375 --> 00:14:26,791
A-Leh, did you just say something?

209
00:14:27,409 --> 00:14:28,409
No.

210
00:14:55,458 --> 00:14:56,458
Hurry!

211
00:15:30,166 --> 00:15:32,366
It doesn't look like there
are any zombies around here.

212
00:15:47,583 --> 00:15:48,333
What do we do?

213
00:15:48,541 --> 00:15:49,541
There's a lot of them.

214
00:15:49,666 --> 00:15:50,666
Conserve your energy.

215
00:17:15,583 --> 00:17:16,583
Brother Li!

216
00:17:16,958 --> 00:17:17,958
Rest in peace.

217
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:22,916
Lin Zai!
